From 743751ecb2dc6b5773d54cb6dfaa5963d1686799 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:45:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(agent): a deleted process cwd no longer crashes
 compaction's system-prompt rebuild

build_context_files_prompt (and list_context_file_sources) fell back to a bare os.getcwd()
when no cwd was configured. A Kanban worker whose workspace dir was removed and recreated
mid-run keeps a cwd on a deleted inode, so the compaction boundary's prompt rebuild raised
FileNotFoundError and killed the worker.

Add runtime_cwd.process_cwd_or_fallback(): the process cwd, else the first existing of the
scope's TERMINAL_CWD, HERMES_KANBAN_WORKSPACE, $HOME, with one warning per process. Route
resolve_agent_cwd and every other agent/ os.getcwd() (coding_context, subdirectory_hints,
tool_executor checkpoint, codex app-server session, lsp cli, trace_upload) through it, and
extend the bare-getcwd guard test from tools/ to all of agent/.
